    "propagation_artefact": "cartservice->adservice was recorded once with a 101737 ms offset. That is not causal propagation; it is a coincidental co-failure inside a long incident window, and it exposes a limitation of defining a propagation edge as any service failing between onset and recovery.",
    "censored_duration_agreement_is_an_artefact": "All held-out incidents use tau=45 s, so the censoring bound is a near-constant 135 s. The corpus contains 31 censored records with median duration 135.5 s. A memory of ~135 s censored records will predict ~135 s for the same cells irrespective of understanding, so the 10/10 directional agreement is NOT independent evidence of accuracy and is not reported as such.",
    "novel_combination_subset": {
      "n": 4,
      "mae_s": 17.4,
      "note": "uncensored held-out incidents whose (fault,service,action) combination never appears in the corpus; MAE 17.4 s against 14.9 s overall, so accuracy roughly holds out of combination, on a very small sample."
    },
    "blast_result_caveat": "Online Boutique propagates deterministically along a fixed call graph and the corpus contains many incidents at the same origins, so Jaccard 0.986 and origin/intermediate detection of 1.0 reflect a largely deterministic mapping rather than hard generalisation.",
    "ranking_caveat": "Ranking separates effective from ineffective actions largely because censored cells sit near 135 s and effective ones near 78-86 s. The estimator learned that separation from censored corpus records, so this demonstrates it identifies ineffective actions, not that it estimates their true (unbounded) duration.",
    "deploy_misconfig_not_rankable": "Two of three deploy_misconfig action cells (pod_restart, scale_replicas) were lost to the 6 no_steady_pre aborts, so that fault group has one measured cell and cannot be ranked."
  }
